    "explore": {
      "text": "Play C, then the very next key up, black or white. Then play C again, skip one key, and play the one after. Which step feels smaller?",
      "instrument": "keyboard",
      "exhibit": {
        "kind": "keyboard",
        "highlight": [
          "C4",
          "C#4",
          "D4"
        ],
        "low": "C4",
        "high": "C5"
      },
      "goal": "Play C to the very next key up, then C to the key after that."
    },
    "name": {
      "cards": [
        {
          "text": "The step from one key to the very next key, black or white, is a [[semitone|semitone]]: the smallest step in music. C to C♯ is a [[semitone|semitone]]. So is E to F, because no key sits between them. The two creeping notes of the *Jaws* theme are a [[semitone|semitone]] apart.",
          "exhibit": {
            "kind": "keyboard",
            "highlight": [
              "E4",
              "F4"
            ],
            "low": "C4",
            "high": "C5"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Skip one key and you have moved a [[tone|tone]], which is 2 [[semitone|semitones]]. C to D is a [[tone|tone]]: the black key C♯ sits in between. A [[semitone|semitone]] has no key in between. A [[tone|tone]] skips one.",
          "exhibit": {
            "kind": "keyboard",
            "highlight": [
              "C4",
              "D4"
            ],
            "low": "C4",
            "high": "C5"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Most neighbouring white keys have a black key between them, so most white-to-white steps are [[tone|tones]]. Only E to F and B to C have no black key. Those two are the white-to-white [[semitone|semitones]].",
          "exhibit": {
            "kind": "keyboard",
            "highlight": [
              "E4",
              "F4",
              "B4",
              "C5"
            ],
            "low": "C4",
            "high": "C5"
          }
        }
      ],
      "alternative": {
        "text": "Think of stairs. Each key, black or white, is one stair. A [[semitone|semitone]] is one stair up. A [[tone|tone]] is two stairs, skipping one. From G, one stair up is G♯ and two stairs up is A, so G to A is a [[tone|tone]]. Listen to the two steps below.",
        "exhibit": {
